items.body:
This is really unfortunate, I did investigate why this was necessary and found that adding;
```c
// Test a function where the name is longer and the linter
// places the function name on the next line, this resulted in
// 'AOTI_TORCH_EXPORT AOTITorchError' being gobbled up by the
// parser.
#if TORCH_FEATURE_VERSION >= TORCH_VERSION_2_12_0
AOTI_TORCH_EXPORT AOTITorchError
this_is_a_very_long_function(StableIValue** ret_value);
#endif // TORCH_FEATURE_VERSION >= TORCH_VERSION_2_12_0

```

to the [sample_shim.h](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/43eaba0456680ba31f758708cc944aea029c6f0d/tools/test/stable_shim_usage_linter_data/sample_shim.h) file still has the stable shim usage test passing, so it fails to pick up `this_is_a_very_long_function`. 

The functions fails to be picked up because `AOTI_TORCH_EXPORT AOTITorchError` is on a different line than the `this_is_a_very_long_function` name. I tried fixing it, but it was more involved than adding a `flags=re.DOTALL` to the matcher. I think the problem needs to be fixed in the `PreprocessorTracker`, but that's really beyond the scope of this PR.

